.g-config-breadcrumb-container

form.g-oidc-config-form(role="form")
  .form-group
    .checkbox
      label
        input.g-oidc-enabled(type="checkbox", checked=config.enabled)
        |  Enable OIDC login
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-client-id") Client ID
    input#g-oidc-client-id.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.clientId)
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-client-secret") Client secret
    input#g-oidc-client-secret.input-sm.form-control(type="password", autocomplete="new-password",
        placeholder=config.clientSecretSet ? "(unchanged — leave blank to keep)" : "")
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-public-url") Provider URL (issuer, browser-facing)
    input#g-oidc-public-url.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.publicUrl,
        placeholder="https://idp.example.com/realms/myrealm")
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-internal-url") Internal provider URL (optional)
    input#g-oidc-internal-url.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.internalUrl,
        placeholder="Server-to-server URL; leave blank if same as above")
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-scopes") Scopes
    input#g-oidc-scopes.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.scopes,
        placeholder="openid profile email")
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-button-label") Login button label
    input#g-oidc-button-label.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.buttonLabel)
  .form-group
    .checkbox
      label
        input.g-oidc-auto-create(type="checkbox", checked=config.autoCreateUsers)
        |  Automatically create Girder accounts for new identities
  .form-group
    .checkbox
      label
        input.g-oidc-ignore-registration(type="checkbox", checked=config.ignoreRegistrationPolicy)
        |  Ignore closed registration policy
  .form-group
    .checkbox
      label
        input.g-oidc-trust-unverified-email(type="checkbox", checked=config.trustUnverifiedEmail)
        |  Trust the email claim even without <code>email_verified</code>
    p.g-oidc-field-help Off by default. Girder matches and creates accounts by email address, so with this on anyone who can set an address at the provider can claim the matching Girder account. Only enable it for a provider that verifies every address it emits but omits the claim.
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-required-claim") Required claim (optional)
    input#g-oidc-required-claim.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.requiredClaim,
        placeholder="e.g. groups, or resource_access.girder.roles")
    p.g-oidc-field-help Restricts who may sign in. When set, an identity is refused unless its ID token carries this claim &mdash; no account is created and no session is issued. Dots descend into nested claims, so <code>resource_access.girder.roles</code> reads a keycloak per-client role. Leave blank to admit every identity the provider authenticates.
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-required-claim-value") Required claim value (optional)
    input#g-oidc-required-claim-value.input-sm.form-control(type="text",
        value=config.requiredClaimValue, placeholder="Required value, e.g. access")
    p.g-oidc-field-help For a list claim (groups/roles) this is the required member; for a scalar, the required value. Leave blank to match any truthy value.
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-admin-claim") Admin claim (optional)
    input#g-oidc-admin-claim.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.adminClaim,
        placeholder="e.g. groups, roles, or is_admin")
    p.g-oidc-field-help ID-token claim that grants site-admin. On each login the admin flag is synced to match this claim (granted or revoked). Leave blank to disable.
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-admin-claim-value") Admin claim value (optional)
    input#g-oidc-admin-claim-value.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.adminClaimValue,
        placeholder="Required value, e.g. girder-admins")
    p.g-oidc-field-help For a list claim (groups/roles) this is the required member; for a scalar, the required value. Leave blank to match any truthy value (e.g. a boolean claim).
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-groups-claim") Groups claim (optional)
    input#g-oidc-groups-claim.input-sm.form-control(type="text", value=config.groupsClaim,
        placeholder="e.g. groups, or resource_access.girder.roles")
    p.g-oidc-field-help Mirrors the provider's groups into Girder groups, so they can be used in the access control list of a collection or folder like any other group. Each value of the claim gets a Girder group, created on first sight; membership is reconciled at each login. Groups you create by hand in Girder are never modified. Leave blank to disable.
  .form-group
    label.control-label(for="g-oidc-group-name-prefix") Mirrored group name prefix (optional)
    input#g-oidc-group-name-prefix.input-sm.form-control(type="text",
        value=config.groupNamePrefix, placeholder="e.g. \"IdP: \"")
    p.g-oidc-field-help Put in front of the claim value when a group is created. If a Girder group of that name already exists and is not one of ours, the claim value is ignored rather than taken over &mdash; a prefix keeps the two name spaces apart.
  .form-group
    .checkbox
      label
        input.g-oidc-groups-authoritative(type="checkbox", checked=config.groupsAuthoritative)
        |  The provider owns membership of mirrored groups
    p.g-oidc-field-help On by default: a user whose token no longer carries a group is removed from it at their next login. Turn it off to only ever add. A token that carries no groups claim at all never revokes anything &mdash; that is a misconfigured provider, not an empty group list.
  .g-oidc-redirect-uri-container
    b Redirect URI to register with your provider:
    span.g-oidc-redirect-uri= redirectUri
  p.g-validation-failed-message#g-oidc-error-message
  .g-oidc-actions
    input.btn.btn-sm.btn-primary.g-oidc-save(type="submit", value="Save")
    button.btn.btn-sm.btn-default.g-oidc-test(type="button")
      i.icon-link-ext
      |  Test connection
  .g-oidc-test-result#g-oidc-test-result
